First, let's determine the number of jewels Raymond has.

Raymond has 40 jewels.
Aaron has 5 more jewels than half of Raymond's jewels.
Half of Raymond's jewels is 40 / 2 = 20 jewels.
Aaron has 5 more jewels than this, so Aaron has 20 + 5 = 25 jewels.

Now, let's find out how many jewels Siobhan has.

Siobhan has 2 fewer jewels than Aaron.
Aaron has 25 jewels.
So, Siobhan has 25 - 2 = 23 jewels.

#### 23 [end of text]


